## MANDATORY UI TESTING RULES

### 1. Color Contrast Check (CRITICAL!)
**NEVER create invisible elements!** Always verify:
- Text is readable against background
- Buttons/links are visible WITHOUT hover
- Icons have sufficient contrast

```python
# Check element visibility BEFORE and AFTER hover
element = page.locator('[data-testid="menu-toggle"]')
# Screenshot in normal state
page.screenshot(path='/tmp/before_hover.png')
# Screenshot on hover
element.hover()
page.screenshot(path='/tmp/after_hover.png')
# BOTH must show the element clearly!
```

**BAD (invisible until hover):**
```css
.menu-btn { color: #333; background: #333; } /* INVISIBLE! */
.menu-btn:hover { color: #fff; }
```

**GOOD (always visible):**
```css
.menu-btn { color: #fff; background: #333; } /* Always visible */
.menu-btn:hover { background: #555; }
```

### Color Contrast Rules (MANDATORY!)

**RULE:** Text MUST have sufficient contrast with the background.

#### Minimum Contrast per Background:

| Background | Minimum Text Color | Examples |
|------------|---------------------|--------------|
| **White/Light** (`#fff`, `bg-white`, `bg-gray-50`) | Dark (`#111`, `#333`, `text-gray-900`) | ✅ `text-gray-900` ❌ `text-gray-500` |
| **Dark** (`#000`, `bg-gray-900`, `bg-black`) | White/Light (`#fff`, `text-white`) | ✅ `text-white` ❌ `text-gray-400` |
| **Colored** (purple, blue, green bg) | White or very dark | ✅ `text-white` on `bg-purple-600` |

#### Tailwind Specific Rules:

| Class | Contrast on White | Use? |
|-------|-------------------|------|
| `text-gray-900` | ✅ Excellent | YES - for main text |
| `text-gray-800` | ✅ Good | YES - for main text |
| `text-gray-700` | ⚠️ Medium | ONLY for secondary text |
| `text-gray-600` | ⚠️ Low | AVOID on white - use on gray-100+ |
| `text-gray-500` | ❌ Poor | NO - not clearly visible |
| `text-gray-400` | ❌ Very Poor | NO - almost invisible |

#### CSS/HEX Rules:

| Text Color | Min Background Brightness |
|------------|---------------------------|
| `#333` / `rgb(51,51,51)` | Lighter than `#ccc` |
| `#666` / `rgb(102,102,102)` | ⚠️ Only on `#f5f5f5` or lighter |
| `#999` / `rgb(153,153,153)` | ❌ NEVER on white |
| `#fff` / `white` | Darker than `#666` |

#### WCAG 2.1 Quick Reference:
- **Normal text:** 4.5:1 contrast ratio minimum
- **Large text (18px+):** 3:1 contrast ratio minimum
- **Icons/Graphics:** 3:1 contrast ratio minimum

**Tool for checking:** https://webaim.org/resources/contrastchecker/

